# How old is the typical person? Niger, Brazil, the US, Italy and Japan
subtitle: "Place five countries on a line by the age of their middle person, then see why Japan, the oldest, was younger in 1950 than Brazil is today."
tags: ["geography","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Half of Niger is under 15\" note \"Japan: ?\""

## How old is the typical person? Niger, Brazil, the US, Italy and Japan
feedback:
    style: warm
    perfect: A demographer in the making.
    good: A sharp sense of the world's ages.
    poor: The world is younger and older than it looks.
    none: Ages hide well. Now you know them.
page: {"valign":"none"}
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Median age
      authors: Our World in Data, from UN World Population Prospects 2024
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/median-age
      finding: 'median age in 2023: Niger 15.3, Brazil 33.9, United States 38.0, Italy 47.5, Japan 49.0, world 30.4; Japan 21.3 in 1950'
    - id: wpp
      title: World Population Prospects 2024
      authors: United Nations, Population Division
      year: 2024
      finding: 'medium projection: Niger''s median age passes 30 around 2082'

    scale age cites ["owid"] x 90 y 390 width 820 unit " yrs" min 10 max 55 hidden true
    cards lands cites ["owid"] size 1.25 along age hidden true
        * "Niger" icon.of "flag niger" icon.set twemoji value 15.3
        * "Brazil" icon.of "flag brazil" icon.set twemoji value 33.9
        * "USA" icon.of "flag united states" icon.set twemoji value 38
        * "Italy" icon.of "flag italy" icon.set twemoji value 47.5
        * "Japan" icon.of "flag japan" icon.set twemoji value 49
    dot pt_ner #b5482e at.x 186.57777777777778 at.y 390 hidden true
    text n_ner "15" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 186.57777777777778 y 302 font_size 40 hidden true
    dot pt_bra #b5482e at.x 525.5111111111112 at.y 390 hidden true
    text n_bra "34" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 525.5111111111112 y 302 font_size 40 hidden true
    dot pt_usa #b5482e at.x 600.2222222222222 at.y 390 hidden true
    text n_usa "38" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 600.2222222222222 y 302 font_size 40 hidden true
    dot pt_ita #b5482e at.x 773.3333333333334 at.y 390 hidden true
    text n_ita "47" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 759.3333333333334 y 302 font_size 40 hidden true
    dot pt_jpn #b5482e at.x 800.6666666666666 at.y 390 hidden true
    text n_jpn "49" #b5482e cites ["owid"] x 814.6666666666666 y 302 font_size 40 hidden true
    arrow gap_arrow #b5482e from.x 186.57777777777778 from.y 262 to.x 800.6666666666666 to.y 262 hidden true
    text gap_l "34 years older" #b5482e x 500 y 222 font_size 44 hidden true
    dot world_pt #8a5fa8 at.x 461.73333333333335 at.y 390 hidden true
    text world_l "World: 30" #8a5fa8 cites ["owid"] x 461.73333333333335 y 222 font_size 48 hidden true
    dot jp50_pt #2f6b8f at.x 295.9111111111111 at.y 390 hidden true
    arrow jp50_arrow dashed #2f6b8f from.x 800.6666666666666 from.y 262 to.x 301.9111111111111 to.y 262 hidden true
    text jp50_l "Japan 1950: 21" #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] x 385.9111111111111 y 222 font_size 48 hidden true

    card title "How old is the typical person?"

How old is the typical person in a country? Line everyone up by age and take the one in the middle: that is the median age.
    draw age

Here are five countries, from Africa, South America, North America, Europe and Asia.
    draw lands

    ask "Drag each country to its median age on the line." on lands store w tolerance 0.08
        right: All {w.total} close.
        wrong: {w.within} of {w.total} close.

Here are the true ages: from about fifteen in Niger to forty-nine in Japan.
    draw pt_ner n_ner pt_bra n_bra pt_usa n_usa pt_ita n_ita pt_jpn n_jpn parallel true

Niger is one of the youngest countries on Earth: half its people are children.
    highlight n_ner effect circle

So Japan's middle person is thirty-four years older than Niger's.
    draw gap_arrow gap_l

    erase gap_arrow gap_l

And the whole world sits between them, at about thirty.
    draw world_pt world_l

    erase world_l

But Japan was not always old. In 1950, its median age was twenty-one.
    draw jp50_arrow jp50_pt jp50_l

That is younger than Brazil is today.
    highlight lands_2

Fewer babies and much longer lives aged Japan by nearly thirty years in seven decades.
    highlight jp50_arrow

    erase jp50_arrow jp50_l jp50_pt

Niger is on the same road, only later: the UN expects its median age to pass thirty around 2082.
    arrow ner_arrow dashed #2f6b8f from.x 186.57777777777778 from.y 262 to.x 458.0888888888889 to.y 262
    text ner_l "Niger ~2082: 30" #2f6b8f cites ["wpp"] x 308.66666666666663 y 222 font_size 46

So one of the youngest countries today may one day be as old as the whole world is now.
    text same "= world today" #8a5fa8 x 611.7333333333333 y 222 font_size 46

